        "title": "Roman Rhetoric",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Cicero (106–43 BCE) is the most important figure in Latin literature and the greatest Roman orator. His rhetorical theory is developed across multiple works; the mature synthesis is *De Oratore* (55 BCE)."
    },
