        "root_concepts": "[roman, rhetoric]",
        "section": "rhetoric",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Roman Rhetoric",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "STASIS THEORY (from Hermagoras):\n  The core analytical tool for forensic rhetoric.\n  Before you can argue a case, identify the STASIS —\n  the point at issue, the exact question in dispute."
    },
    {
      "id": "02-ROMAN-RHETORIC.md#016",
      "path": [
        "02-ROMAN-RHETORIC.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:rhetoric:02-roman-rhetoric, git-history:rhetoric:02-roman-rhetoric]",
        "canonical_path": "rhetoric/02-ROMAN-RHETORIC.md",
        "concepts": "[roman, rhetoric]",
        "current_path": "rhetoric/02-ROMAN-RHETORIC.md",
        "id": "maxim:rhetoric:roman-rhetoric",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "rhetoric",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[roman, rhetoric]",
        "section": "rhetoric",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Roman Rhetoric",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "FOUR TYPES OF STASIS:\n  1. Conjectural stasis (an sit): did the act happen?\n     \"Did he kill her?\" — a question of fact.\n  2. Definitional stasis (quid sit): what kind of act is it?\n     \"Was it murder or self-defense?\" — a question of definition.\n  3. Qualitative stasis (quale sit): what is its moral character?\n     \"Even if he did it — was it justified?\" — a question of quality.\n  4. Translative stasis (translation): should this court\n     hear this case? — a jurisdictional question."
    }
  ],
